    "image_text_Rr8iJJ": {
      "type": "image-text",
      "blocks": {
        "images_NXFXtC": {
          "type": "images",
          "settings": {
            "image_one": "shopify://shop_images/Bedroom_Four_19_of_22.jpg"
          }
        },
        "content_c9CaD6": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "title": "",
            "title_size": "xl",
            "text": "Unusually Short Timeframe\nWoolton Acre has been completed to exacting standards despite the unusually short timeframe available. Having acquired the property, the new owners completed the turnaround with minimum delay. In mid-December 2023, Furncare were invited to bid to furnish all 48 bedrooms and communal areas, including the lounges, dining rooms, day clinic, bar area, quiet rooms, isolation room and corridors.\n\nLook & Feel of a Bespoke Designer Solution\nDetailed interior design proposals were developed at Furncare and even suggested decorative specifications and lighting schematics to ensure every room was bright, light and safe. The plans had the look and feel of a bespoke designer solution, but all the care home interiors were from stock and guarantees were provided assuring delivery within days of confirmation.\n\nThe contract was signed in January 2024 and all 1,831 items ordered were delivered from the Furncare National Distribution Centre. The order was installed in each room just days later in the first week of February.",
            "button_style": "underline",
            "button_text": "",
            "button_url": ""
          }
        }
      },
